jitXscRT -- AN AND/OR OPERAND THAT EMITS NOTHING UNDER JIT (SEQ 335 R2, fault A). 2026-10-11.

`*fId(x)` is a star on a call target: the jit has no emit for it (switch off the operand yields no value; switch on the
candidate refuses "a call whose target is built"). So each connective has one operand with no value at emit time:
    xrA = xrL && *fId(xrR);     the RIGHT operand
    xrB = *fId(xrL) || xrR;     the LEFT operand -- and its value is decided by xrR, so fire 2 must read 1
jitEmitShortCircuit now clears the value in flight before each operand and runs an operand with no value as ONE run-time
call (jitScOperandRT, interpreted). Before that fix the right case read the stale assignment (9) and the left case omitted
the connective entirely, so xrB read back its own tag. The interpreted oracle runs last, after the jitted fires
(bear-trap 25), on both input sets.
Wanted: fire 1 = interpreted 1 = 0 0; fire 2 = interpreted 2 = 0 1. The degrade count is 2 -- two named fallbacks, and the
values are what say they were sound (the degrade doctrine: a degrade line asserts a fallback occurred, never that it was).
